brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
make a bluesky bot that jumps into random tech/ai posts (prefer intense or focused convos) and recommends everyone involved log off, touch grass, reconnect with their senses, etc in a condescending paternalist tone @buildthis.bisks.net

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@brennan.computer: +1 totally believe this -- I'm old enough to remember CPU image rendering where each frame was 1-2 hours and you'd make a change, wait, make a change, wait...

and then the first GPU rendering came out, and now it's ~real time and you just flyyy
  [quoting @joetforhire.com: heard devs talk ab "losing flow state" due to waiting for ai completions now. i suspect zero latency replies will change that. as a frequent ai-enabled flow state enjoyer, i think instant frontier-class outputs will feel like ascending into nirvana]
@hetkey.bsky.social: After 35 years in the IT industry

I can honestly say it’s better just to go outside and stand by a tree

Nothing we create fails to be obsolete within a moment of creating it

Step away from the screen and start enjoying the beautiful world we live in before it’s gone.
@brennan.computer: ...what?
@hetkey.bsky.social: You heard me.
